= School Safety: Specific Threats, Measurable Countermeasures
<school-safety-specific-threats-measurable-countermeasures>
Defensive readiness without compromising constitutional rights or public
trust

#cover-note[
#cover-note[
Publication 17.0 Revision 1. Editorial corrections and verifiable
advisory reasoning; independent acceptance and site validation remain
pending.

]
]
]
#text-block[
Approve a scenario-based qualification program, not a technology
shopping list. Assess credible threats to students, protect lawful
ownership, and fund only controls that demonstrate a protective purpose
and do not create unacceptable new hazards.

]
#callout[
#strong[First and Second Amendment safeguards.] Protect lawful expression, religious exercise, peaceful assembly, association, petitions and lawful firearm ownership. Political viewpoint, criticism of officials, lawful advocacy and lawful ownership alone must not trigger threat labels, surveillance or adverse action. Require corroborated conduct, documented legal authority, independent human review and an accessible correction/appeal route.
]

== Five immediate decisions
<five-immediate-decisions>
+ #strong[Require a traceable threat register.] Give every concern an
  observable condition, independent corroboration, response authority,
  outcome metric and sunset criterion.
+ #strong[Support voluntary secure storage.] Offer families storage
  education and equipment referrals without collecting firearm-owner
  identities.
+ #strong[Verify initial-minutes protective capability.] Independently
  exercise alerts, classroom egress, accessible communications, bleeding
  control, and dispatch coordination.
+ #strong[Separate established controls from exploratory technology.]
  Permit small offline pilots of sensors, canines and AI, but do not
  equate promising capabilities with verified reductions in shooting
  casualties.
+ #strong[Make G0 governance non-waivable.] Set clear legal authority,
  restrictions on sharing student records, independent complaint review,
  and penalties for retaliatory or selective use.

